  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEVEL OF A PACIFIC AMERICAS FLYWAY SHOREBIRD CONSERVATION BUSINESS PLAN I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal is for Phase I of a two-year project to develop a Pacific Americas Flyway Shorebird Conservation Business Plan. In Phase I, we propose to convene an international planning committee to develop and refine a conceptual model with input from key partners in Central and South America, Mexico, the United States and Canada. We will use the methods of the Open Standards for the Practice of Conservation, including the Miradi model-building software, and convene two workshops for partner input. Phase II will include the completion and publication of the full Pacific Americas Shorebird Conservation Business Plan. Based on the success of other flyway strategies, we believe a comprehensive flyway approach is the only way to effectively conserve long-distance migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
